#4471 is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own reports say otherwise. Read by tenant
and by the way each report came in, not by subject line, they hold three different problems.
Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix does not close #4471. Two of its problems are not in the parser.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/Domakonda/MegaDev/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/Domakonda/MegaDev/issues/2',
    'one-day-move': 'https://github.com/Domakonda/MegaDev/issues/3',
  }}
/>

## The three problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day first,
  so "4 March" comes out as "3 April". These come in by app and email, and by form from tenants
  on booking-v2, whose hint is right.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint
  tells them, and the form reads it day first. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants. The
  parser fix leaves this one as it is.
- **`one-day-move`**: the date moves by one day, not a swap: Tuesday becomes Monday, a client in
  Lisbon and one in Toronto get different days for the same meeting, an invite arrives before the
  booking. A month-first parser cannot do that. It points to time zones. The desk noted these
  reports in `desk-notes.json`; the table on the #4471 page still files them under `parser`.

## Why one ticket hid them

- Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. All three
  problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Dates mixed up"), so they
  landed in one ticket.
- Intake's `hint` tag follows the reporter's browser, not the tenant. It marks US-English
  browsers as `hint`, and misses real `hint` reports from local browsers. Count by tenant and
  channel (`causes.ts`), never by tag.
- The export repeats reports across its pages. Count each id once (`uniqueById`).

## What to do now

1. Work each ticket on its own; close #4471 only when all three are fixed.
2. Replace decision 0001 with a new record: merge on cause, not on subject.

